Welcome to the Secret Santa generator website's repository.  This ReadMe will explain how to use the site.

There's one page to this site which handles all parts of the Secret Santa generator.  The first part is the text area inputs; the second is the buttons below the text areas.  There are three text areas on the landing page - list of participants, list of previous pairings and list of participant emails.  These text areas control who is taking part in the event, who those participants cannot get from the prior year and notifying them of who they'll be buying for in the current/upcoming event.  These fields must follow the below formats, otherwise the generator won't work:
- List of Participants: list each participant's name in a list format => a, b, c, ...
- List of Previous Pairings: list each previous pairing in a mapping format => a:b, b:c, c:d, ...
    - if a new person is added, you can exclude them from this section; the generator will just make sure they don't get themselves this year
- List of Participant Emails: list each participant's name and their email in a mapping format => a:a@gmail.com, b:b@outlook.com, ...
    - if a person does not have an email, you must put their name in, but can leave the email part of the mapping empty.  A link will be generated for you to send to that person separately => a:, b:b@gmail.com, ...

Below these text areas on the landing page is two buttons: "Pair Participants" and "Send Notification".  Upon clicking the "Pair Participants" button, the participants listed in the participants text area will be randomly matched with someone who isn't themselves nor is the person listed as their "previous person" in the previous pairings text area.  The purpose of this is to avoid getting the same person multiple years in a row, for good or bad.  Once the pairings have been made, an alert will pop up stating the pairings are done, and the "Send Notification" button will then become enabled.
Upon clicking the "Send Notification" button, the participants listed in the participants text area will be notified by email about who they got for the event, using the emails listed in the participant emails text area.  This notification message will also include a link to the group's google doc that lists each person's gift preferences and address for shipping (shipping only applies to the participant if the person they're getting a gift(s) for is unable to attend the event in person).

reference: https://codepen.io/jak_e/pen/Pxvzwv